  "content": {
    "id": "p13-g43-48-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "43",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of the term indicated in the following expansions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(1+x)^8(2+x)^4$; term indicated: $x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$728$.",
          "worked": "Match powers $0+2$, $1+1$ and $2+0$. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\binom{4}{2}2^2+8\\binom{4}{1}2^3+\\binom{8}{2}2^4\\\\C&=24+256+448\\\\C&=728\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(2+x)(3x+1)^4$; term indicated: $x^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$270$.",
          "worked": "Match powers $0+3$ and $1+2$. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=2\\binom{4}{3}3^3+\\binom{4}{2}3^2\\\\C&=216+54\\\\C&=270\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(3-x)^5(1+x)^7$; term indicated: $x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2538$.",
          "worked": "Match powers $0+2$, $1+1$ and $2+0$. Let $C_{i,j}$ denote the contribution from powers $i$ and $j$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_{0,2}&=3^5\\binom{7}{2}=5103\\\\C_{1,1}&=-\\binom{5}{1}3^4\\binom{7}{1}=-2835\\\\C_{2,0}&=\\binom{5}{2}3^3=270\\\\C&=5103-2835+270=2538\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(5-x)^2(1+2x)^5$; term indicated: $x^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1610$.",
          "worked": "Since $(5-x)^2=25-10x+x^2$, match these terms with powers three, two and one in the second factor. Let $C$ be the required coefficient.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=25\\binom{5}{3}2^3-10\\binom{5}{2}2^2+\\binom{5}{1}2\\\\C&=2000-400+10\\\\C&=1610\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(4+3x)^6(2+5x)^4$; term indicated: $x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\,959\\,680$.\n\nAdd the three contributions with total degree two.",
          "worked": "Match powers $0+2$, $1+1$ and $2+0$. Let $C_{i,j}$ denote the contribution from powers $i$ and $j$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_{0,2}&=4^6\\binom{4}{2}2^2 5^2=2\\,457\\,600\\\\C_{1,1}&=\\binom{6}{1}4^5 3\\binom{4}{1}2^3 5\\\\C_{1,1}&=2\\,949\\,120\\\\C_{2,0}&=\\binom{6}{2}4^4 3^2 2^4=552\\,960\\\\C&=2\\,457\\,600+2\\,949\\,120+552\\,960\\\\C&=5\\,959\\,680\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-g43-48-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(7-2x)^5(3-x)^6$; term indicated: $x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$65\\,428\\,965$.\n\nAdd the three contributions with total degree two; each contribution is positive.",
          "worked": "Match powers $0+2$, $1+1$ and $2+0$. Let $C_{i,j}$ denote the contribution from powers $i$ and $j$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C_{0,2}&=7^5\\binom{6}{2}3^4=20\\,420\\,505\\\\C_{1,1}&=\\binom{5}{1}7^4(-2)\\binom{6}{1}3^5(-1)\\\\C_{1,1}&=35\\,006\\,580\\\\C_{2,0}&=\\binom{5}{2}7^3(-2)^2 3^6\\\\C_{2,0}&=10\\,001\\,880\\\\C&=20\\,420\\,505+35\\,006\\,580+10\\,001\\,880\\\\C&=65\\,428\\,965\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
